content:
{
  "asset": "P-114 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-20500, raw-water transfer line",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "The reported drive-end bearing-housing vibration of 8.3 mm/s exceeds the applicable HF-300 Zone C/D boundary of 7.1 mm/s RMS and falls within Figure 3 Zone D, 7.1–11.0 mm/s RMS: 'Damage likely – stop the pump'. This is the manufacturer's highest severity zone, so SSP-07 requires an immediate stop and notification of the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The housing temperature of 70 °C is at the HF-300's documented upper normal limit of 70 °C, below the 80 °C alarm and 90 °C trip; the manual specifies housing-surface temperature measurement. Because 70 °C is not above the manufacturer's alarm limit, SSP-07's temperature-based requirement to raise a priority-1 work order within the shift is not triggered by this reading.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No leakage is reported. The troubleshooting table invokes mechanical-seal replacement for leakage at the shaft seal, so seal replacement is not supported by the current evidence; the high-vibration checks are alignment, bearings, impeller and NPSH.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "P1 is assigned as a planning decision because the pump has an immediate-stop, highest-severity vibration condition, not because of the separate bearing-temperature alarm rule.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Misalignment — listed as a probable cause of high vibration; check alignment. The evidence does not rank the causes, so this sequence follows the troubleshooting table and is not a confirmed diagnosis.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear — listed as a probable cause of high vibration; inspect the bearings. The 70 °C reading does not independently establish high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage — listed as a probable cause of high vibration; inspect the impeller.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Cavitation — listed as a probable cause of high vibration; check NPSH.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop P-114 immediately and initiate notification of the reliability engineer. Do not restart until the required notification has been made.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before internal work, electrically isolate and apply lock-out/tag-out at the MCC; mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves; drain and vent first and obtain the line-break permit. Isolate and drain the pump before disassembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before disturbing the motor or bearing housing, check shaft alignment and check NPSH. Record alignment against the section 5.4 tolerances: parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For bearing and impeller inspection, use the back pull-out arrangement, which allows removal of the rotating assembly without disturbing the casing or pipework. The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg and therefore exceeds the 25 kg SSP-07 lifting threshold: use a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C09",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect both bearings and the impeller. If either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature, replace both bearings as a pair: drive-end HF3-512 (6312-C3) and non-drive-end HF3-510 (6310-C3). Do not treat bearing replacement as confirmed solely from the vibration reading.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Install a new HF3-120 casing gasket whenever the casing is opened during this work.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "On reassembly, tighten any disturbed fasteners with lightly oiled threads to Table 5: M16 casing bolts 210 Nm; M24 impeller nut 160 Nm; M10 seal gland nuts 25 Nm; M12 bearing-housing bolts 85 Nm. Apply only the values for fasteners actually disturbed.",
      "citations": [
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, use a laser alignment tool and achieve parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular alignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before restart, confirm that the reliability engineer has been notified. After restart, measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings, classify the highest reading with Figure 3, and stop the pump again if the highest reading is in Zone D; thereafter maintain the specified weekly both-housing monitoring.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3; conditional—use as one of the required pair if either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3; conditional—replace together with the drive-end bearing when pair replacement is triggered.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; replace whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Highest-severity vibration control: stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Internal-pump work controls: electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanical isolation of suction and discharge valves, and a line-break permit with draining and venting completed first.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Lifting control for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly: a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment are required because the component exceeds 25 kg.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The chemical goggles and nitrile-gloves control is not triggered by the supplied scope: that control concerns chemically dosed lines, while the documented dosing statement identifies P-101 to P-106 on the filtered-water line, not P-114 on the raw-water transfer line.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Conditional bearing replacement as a pair, if inspection confirms the replacement trigger: 6.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional laser alignment after work moves the motor or bearing housing: 1.5 hours with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "No conflicting limits or instructions are present in the supplied chunks. AquaDyne AQ-OM-300 Revision D is the model-specific source for this HF-300, while SSP-07 Revision 3 applies to all site pumps; their stop requirements are complementary. No alternative serial-range or date-specific limit is supplied, so no serial/date precedence decision is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C07",
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "The report does not explicitly state that the 8.3 mm/s reading is RMS and provides no non-drive-end vibration reading. Confirm the measurement convention and measure both bearing housings so the highest reading can be classified as required; this verification must not delay the immediate-stop action for the reported Zone D value. (C06, C07)",
    "The actual cause and whether bearing-pair replacement is necessary remain unconfirmed until the alignment, NPSH, bearing and impeller checks are completed. (C09, C10)",
    "No NPSH acceptance value or site NPSH calculation/data is supplied, so cavitation cannot be assessed quantitatively from the evidence. (C09)",
    "Table 6 gives no standard hours for troubleshooting, NPSH checking, bearing/impeller inspection or inspection-only disassembly and reassembly, so total labour cannot be finalised from the supplied evidence. (C09, C12)",
    "If impeller damage or cavitation is confirmed, the supplied troubleshooting entry does not provide the subsequent repair procedure or required corrective parts; additional technical information will be needed. (C09)"
  ]
}
